// Phatakorva: Mikael Frödin's Temple Dog tube fly, a long fiery brown wing in sections over a short bronze body, with a copper cone.

id phatakorva
name "Phatakorva"
aliases "Pahtakorva" "Phatagorva"
type salmon
imitates attractor
difficulty advanced
species salmon
// Assumption: Heimburg fishes it from spring to autumn; the months of a Scandinavian salmon season.
season may june july august september october
origin originator="Mikael Frödin" region="Sweden"
description "A short body of bronze holo braid and glitz dubbing, an orange craft fur underwing, a long wing of fiery brown soft hair in two sections with copper and bronze angel hair, the front section folded back, an orange badger hackle between them, a long black soft hackle in front, orange peacock herl over the top, jungle cock cheeks and a copper tungsten cone."
history """
    Mikael Frödin's best-known fly, as his own company calls it, spelt Pahtakorva and Phatakorva on
    its pages. Daniel Heimburg traces it to the original Temple Dog of Håkan Norling, Frödin's
    friend. Timo Kontio credits Norling with the Temple Dog style and Frödin with helping to make
    it known: a wing of soft hair in sections, with hackle wound between them, tied flat round the
    tube so that only its underside is left clear, the last section often tied in Norling's
    reversed way, pointing forward and then folded back.

    The dressing here follows the materials of Frödin's Classic Pahtakorva pack, his version close
    to the original, which lists them without an order; the order is the Temple Dog's, as Martin
    Joergensen, Stuart Foxall and Michael Müller give it. Other tyers vary it: Heimburg ties his on
    a short brass tube with fox and tanuki and a black top to the wing, and Tellis Katsogiannos in
    three sections of fiery brown fox with an orange badger hackle and a black hackle between them.
    """
fishing """
    Frödin calls it a standard fly that works everywhere, perhaps best in tea-coloured rivers, its
    medium profile a standard too when a river clears a little. Heimburg fishes it most when the
    water is a little tea-coloured and the clouds are out, and finds it much fished on the Alta.
    Tellis Katsogiannos took his biggest salmon on it, about 16 kg, in September on the Mörrum.
    """
sources {
    "Frödin Flies: Classic Pahtakorva" url="http://web.archive.org/web/20260515174712/https://www.frodinflies.com/products/classic-pahtakorva"
    "Frödin Flies: PM #21 Classic Pahtakorva, material pack" url="http://web.archive.org/web/20260519124413/https://www.frodinflies.com/products/pm-21-classic-pahtakorva"
    "Frödin Flies: Pattern of the month #21, Classic Pahtakorva (film)" url="http://web.archive.org/web/20250523045921/https://www.frodinflies.com/blogs/film-archive/pattern-of-the-month-21-classic-pahtakorva"
    "Laxflugor.nu: Pahtakorva laxfluga (Daniel Heimburg)" url="http://web.archive.org/web/20260616051919/https://laxflugor.nu/laxflugor/pahtakorva-laxfluga/"
    "Tellis Flugfiske: Pahtakorva / Phatagorva (Tellis Katsogiannos)" url="https://tellis-flugfiske.se/2021/12/07/13-pahtakorva-phatagorva/"
    "GlobalFlyFisher: Styles and patterns (Martin Joergensen)" url="https://globalflyfisher.com/node/14316"
    "SwittersB: Mikael Frödin, FITS, Temple Dog wings and tube flies" url="https://swittersb.com/2009/01/01/mikael-frodin-fits-temple-dog-wings-tube-flies/"
    "Fly Tying Archive: Håkan Norling (Timo Kontio)" url="https://flytyingarchive.com/?p=338"
    "Deneki: Fly tying, Black 'n Silver Templedog tube (Stuart Foxall)" url="http://deneki.com/2021/08/fly-tying-black-n-silver-templedog-tube/"
    "Fliegenfischer-Forum: Tubenfliegen (Michael Müller)" url="https://www.fliegenfischer-forum.de/tuben1.html"
}
// Photos for checking proportions while authoring (pnpm refcheck); never published.
references {
    "https://www.frodinflies.com/cdn/shop/products/classic_pahtakorva_4ff1d77c-59a3-47c9-aaf5-1f7c26735cbb_1024x1024.jpg?v=1658769849" page="https://www.frodinflies.com/products/classic-pahtakorva" author="Frödin Flies" license="All rights reserved; reference only" note="The originator's Classic, side view without a hook"
    "https://www.superflies.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/TD-Phatagorva-Templedog-tungsten-conehead_jpg.webp" page="https://www.superflies.com/products/phatakorva-templedog-tungsten-conehead" license="All rights reserved; reference only" note="On a tube pin: the body's proportions"
    "https://guideline-products-production.imgix.net/images/524_22bae50c16-103252-full.jpg?q=70&fit=clip&w=1920&fm=jpg&auto=compress,format" page="https://www.guidelineflyfish.com/en/td-bhatakorva-9-cm" license="All rights reserved; reference only" note="A commercial 9 cm Temple Dog version"
}

// Frödin: M FITS tubing for a fixed hook, flies of 6, 8 and 10 cm. Assumption: an 18 mm tube
// for an 8 cm fly, its wing (read from Frödin's photo) four to five times the dressed tube.
hook tube-plastic length=18 treble=10
thread black size="8/0"

materials {
    body-rear flat-tinsel color="#9a6a32" label="Bronze holo braid"
    body-front dubbing color="#8a5a2a" label="Bronze glitz dubbing"
    underwing craft-fur color="#ff6a14" label="Fire fluo orange craft fur"
    wing-rear fox-hair color="#8a2e14" label="Medium fiery brown soft hair"
    flash-rear krystal-flash color=copper count=10 label="Copper angel hair"
    // Read from Frödin's photo: the hackles reach about a third of the way along the wing.
    hackle-rear cock-hackle color=orange fibre=2 sweep=55 label="Orange badger cock hackle"
    wing-front fox-hair color="#7a2812" label="Large fiery brown soft hair"
    flash-front krystal-flash color="#9a6a32" count=10 label="Bronze angel hair"
    hackle-front hen-hackle color=black fibre=2.4 sweep=60 label="Black soft hackle"
    topping peacock-herl color=orange strands=5 label="Orange-dyed peacock eye herl"
    cheeks jungle-cock label="Synthetic jungle cock"
    // Frödin: an XS copper tungsten half cone. Assumption: about 5 mm across at the back.
    cone tungsten-cone color=copper mm=5
}

// Frödin's pack also has black-dyed pheasant rump; it is left out here, the black soft hackle
// making the black collar the photo shows.
steps {
    attach-thread at=0.3
    wrap-thread to=0.04
    tie-in body-rear
    wrap-thread to=0.28
    wind body-rear to=0.28 turns=8
    tie-off body-rear
    dub body-front to=0.42
    // Read from Frödin's photo: the orange shows under the front third of the wing.
    tie-in underwing length=2.4 angle=4 spread=70 note="A small bunch, combed out."
    // Frödin (SwittersB): the wing flat round the sides of the tube, only its underside clear.
    tie-in wing-rear length=4.4 angle=3 spread=100 note="A small bunch with the underfur combed out, spread round the sides and top."
    trim wing-rear
    // Foxall: the flash a little longer than the hair, to taper the wing.
    tie-in flash-rear length=4.8 angle=3 spread=60 note="A few strands either side."
    tie-in hackle-rear
    wrap-thread to=0.52
    wind hackle-rear to=0.52 turns=3 note="Stroke the fibres back as you wind, so they lift the next section."
    tie-off hackle-rear
    wrap-thread to=0.62
    // GlobalFlyFisher, Müller: the last section tied in pointing forward and folded back.
    tie-in wing-front length=5.6 angle=6 spread=100 forward=#true note="A larger bunch, the butts cut square and bound along the tube."
    pull-over wing-front to=0.62
    tie-in flash-front length=6 angle=5 spread=40
    tie-in hackle-front
    wrap-thread to=0.78
    wind hackle-front to=0.78 turns=3 note="A long, soft collar, stroked back."
    tie-off hackle-front
    tie-in topping length=5.2 angle=6 note="A few strands over the top of the wing."
    // Read from Frödin's photo: about a fifth of the wing's length.
    tie-in cheeks length=1.2 angle=12 spread=35
    whip-finish note="Glue the head."
    slide-bead cone
}
